\chapter{High-Energy Tensor Perturbation Methods}

\section{Shock Injection}
High-energy perturbations are injected:
\[
\Delta T_{\mu\nu} \ge 10^{20}~\text{J/m}^3.
\]

\section{Energy-Momentum Flux}
Flux density is computed using:
\[
F^\mu = T^{\mu\nu} n_\nu,
\]
where $n_\nu$ is the normal vector to the hypersurface.

\section{Metric Drift Analysis}
Metric drift is monitored:
\[
\Delta g_{\mu\nu} = g_{\mu\nu}(t+\Delta t) - g_{\mu\nu}(t).
\]

\section{Stability Conditions}
Stability requires:
\[
\Delta g_{\mu\nu} < 10^{-7}.
\]

