\chapter{Vacuum Extraction Algorithms}

\section{Negative Energy Sinks}
Vacuum extraction arrays remove localized negative energy:
\[
\Theta = \frac{\delta E_{\text{vac}}}{E_{\text{total}}}.
\]

\section{Backreaction Parameter}
Measured:
\[
\Theta = 0.00042,
\qquad
\Theta \le 10^{-3}.
\]

\section{Stability Bounds}
Backreaction stability requires:
\[
\nabla_\mu G^{\mu\nu} = 0.
\]

\section{Vacuum Dynamics}
Vacuum energy contributes:
\[
T_{\text{vac}_q} = \langle 0 | \hat{T}_{\mu\nu} | 0 \rangle.
\]

\section{Unified Evolution}
The unified equation is:
\[
G_{\mu\nu}
= \frac{8\pi G}{c^4}
\left( T_{\mu\nu} + T_{\text{vac}_q} \right).
\]